lledByAPixel/LittleJS","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-07T03:01:12Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"b272aec732ebff2f1974f0e15078b730cbf73306","github_link":"https://github.com/KilledByAPixel/LittleJS/commit/b272aec732ebff2f1974f0e15078b730cbf73306","commit_subject":"Pass 15 #1 to #4, 3D solids: each collider keeps where it was when the pass began (render3DCollideFrom, stamped the first time it moves or is pushed), and a push that would carry one on through the other is turned back by the pair's relative motion from there (render3DPushFrom), so it holds whichever of the two was made first, whichever resolves the pair and whichever moves: a wall made after the player, two movers head on, a mover into one at rest and a platform rising into a box. The settle against fixed solids skips the solid that pushed, ignores a rounding error of overlap and stands as a pair does, after the bounce, so a box on a turned ramp no longer creeps downhill; a crate the wall pushes back hands what it could not move to its pusher, which is settled in turn, so a heavy pusher no longer passes through the crate. The stress room is built with its walls first and last, and the review's scenes are tests, 14 of 15 failing on 1.25.0","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"KilledByAPixel/LittleJS","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-07T03:01:12Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"90fd10696c981317215f9c7ee0e7b3f153471f96","github_link":"https://github.com/KilledByAPixel/LittleJS/commit/90fd10696c981317215f9c7ee0e7b3f153471f96","commit_subject":"Pass 15 P1 and P3: engineObjectsUpdate writes engineCollideGrid only when there is a grid, as V8 keeps a variable never written as a constant and the two writes a frame deoptimized it again and again in every game under 64 solids (41 deopts in 1400 frames, about twice the allocation per frame); hypot is Math.hypot itself, not a function gathering its arguments into an array, and the 3D solid reach writes its length out, as it is asked for every pair (2.5 MB a frame on 300 boxes)","